r-PLS: 0.609

P-value: 0.439

Based on 1000 random permutations
> plot(PLS)

Regardless of ANOVA results, you are not digitizing in a consistent way  There should be some correlation between first and second digitizations.  It could be that your individuals are so familiar that this is bound to happen.  That might be why you are thrown off with the GPA plot.  Try repeating this exercise with knowingly different individuals would help.

Hope that helps!
Mike

