Thank you very much for your explanations. I am aware of the fact that a warning is not an error. I was just wondering that "anova()" returns only the interaction term and not the single factors and whether this might be right. It is true that not every level is interacting with each level of another factor, which is somehow obvious if you have several levels in each factor but some levels occur only a single time, isn´t it?
